<h2 id="why" class="doc-h2">0. Why this document exists</h2>
<p class="doc-body">Availability work was spread across six overlapping documents (~530&nbsp;KB) describing hardware that is not in service. That fragmentation was itself a reliability risk. This v2.0 is the <strong>single source of truth</strong>, rewritten with ONE taxonomy (linear Steps), Kubernetes as the PRIMARY path, and detectability as Step 0.</p>
<div class="doc-info">
    <p class="doc-body"><strong>The single biggest source of confusion - now settled.</strong> The December 2025 plan set named <strong>192.168.1.198</strong> as "the production database" and assumed a 3-host Proxmox cluster. <strong>Both are false today.</strong> Production is bare metal; the primary database is <strong>192.168.1.20:3307</strong> (MariaDB <code>ency</code>). Following those docs would migrate the wrong database on the wrong machines.</p>
</div>
<p class="doc-backtop"><a href="#why">&#8593; Back to Top</a></p>

